  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "The product T-Box (ADR-0015, ADR-0018)",
      "items": [
        "L1, the process: tbox/ovs-concepts.ttl. L0, OVS's own terms: tbox/ovs.ttl.",
        "Lc, per platform and version: what it can do for a step, and how it is obtained (core, edition, plan tier, module, app): capabilities/.",
        "L2, the data model: systems/. Shopify's is generated from its public Admin API schema by generate/shopify_l2.py; Odoo 18.0's terms are checked against the stock source."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "A workspace's outcomes",
      "items": [
        "As-is realisation and target availability, derived on the edge from discovery runs. Availability is never usage.",
        "To-be allocation: a step both sides could do is a decision a person makes, recorded as the workspace's Decision row.",
        "L3: what one deployment changed against its L2 version. Never a tracked file."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Rules that bite",
      "items": [
        "Every rule has a document that must fail it: check.py runs them all.",
        "A-Box rules on every change (shapes/ovs-shapes.ttl); the Map gate once, before Map: every top-level step allocated (shapes/ovs-map-ready.ttl).",
        "All paths are in ovs-dlab5-net, under packages/ontology/."
      ]
    }
  ]
